  "problem": "The second-order initial value problem\n\n$$\n12{y}^{\u2033}+5{y}^{\u2032}-2y=0,\\,y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(1)=-2\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{\u2032}={x}_{2},\\, & {x}_{1}(1)=p \\\\ {x}_{2}^{\u2032}=f(t),\\, & {x}_{2}(1)=q\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{\u2032}(t),$ and $p$ and $q$ are constants. Calculate  $(p-q)\\cdot f(t).$",
